our teams from three Lifeboat stations  in Kent were involved in that  multi-agency operation the rescue in the  channel but of course involved that  fishing vessel that just happened to be  nearby as that inflatable started taking  on water a great panic and as you say  Kent County Council confirming the  really harrowing details of  unaccompanied  youngsters on that vessel that they have  now taken into their care and also  confirming that one of the four who died  was a teenager the process of  identifying those who lost their lives  is still ongoing and of course that  might be quite a difficult process and  might involve contacting families in  different parts of the world so a very  harrowing situation involving young  people we don't know the precise ages of  those who lost their lives or indeed  whether they could be further people who  were lost at sea the search operation  was continuing overnight with drones  being used in the middle of the channel  to try and scour the area very difficult  challenging conditions of course for  those who are out on vessels given the  very very cold temperatures and the rnli  here in Dungeness really paying tribute  to the bravery and compassion of those  on those UK fishing vessels who were  involved and also their Crews who took  part in the rescue and recovery of  people from the water and also the  search process that followed on after  those people who had survived had got  back to shore
 

